      "final_message": "`service2.compute_fee(1000, \"gold\")` returns **480**. Running the function directly gave the same number.\n\nIt only uses two modules:\n1. **`pricing.base_fee(1000)`** is `500 + 1000 // 10`, which is 600.\n2. **`discounts.apply_discount(600, \"gold\")`** takes off gold's 20%: `600 - (600 * 20) // 100`, which is 480.\n\n`decoy_tax.py` and `decoy_shipping.py` aren't imported, so they don't change the result.\n\nANSWER: 480",
